From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:00:00 +0000
Subject: wireless: uwe5622: do not cancel the loopcheck work from itself

When the firmware misses a loopcheck ack, loopcheck_work_queue() calls
stop_loopcheck(), which does cancel_delayed_work_sync() on the work that
is running it and waits forever. The CP2 reset that should follow never
happens, and the next stop_loopcheck() (marlin_cp2_reset() from a WLAN
command timeout) blocks behind it too: WLAN and Bluetooth stay dead
until reboot, with hung task reports for both workers.

Seen on an Orange Pi Zero2 after an SDIO CMD53 timeout under full
system load.

Clear the open bit and complete the waiter without the synchronous
cancel when stopping from the work itself.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/platform/loopcheck.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/platform/loopcheck.c
@@ -51,6 +51,8 @@
 }
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_WCN_LOOPCHECK
+static bool loopcheck_clear_open(void);
+
 static void loopcheck_work_queue(struct work_struct *work)
 {
 	int ret;
@@ -68,7 +70,9 @@
 	if (!test_bit(WCN_LOOPCHECK_OPEN, &loopcheck.status))
 		return;
 	if (!timeleft) {
-		stop_loopcheck();
+		/* stop_loopcheck() would wait for this work to finish */
+		if (!loopcheck_clear_open())
+			return;
 		WCN_ERR("didn't get loopcheck ack\n");
 		WCN_INFO("start dump CP2 mem\n");
 		mdbg_assert_interface("loopcheck fail");
@@ -203,14 +207,20 @@
 	queue_delayed_work(loopcheck.workqueue, &loopcheck.work, HZ);
 }
 
-void stop_loopcheck(void)
+static bool loopcheck_clear_open(void)
 {
 	if (!test_bit(WCN_LOOPCHECK_INIT, &loopcheck.status) ||
 	    !test_and_clear_bit(WCN_LOOPCHECK_OPEN, &loopcheck.status))
-		return;
-	WCN_INFO("%s\n", __func__);
+		return false;
+	WCN_INFO("stop_loopcheck\n");
 	complete_all(&loopcheck.completion);
-	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&loopcheck.work);
+	return true;
+}
+
+void stop_loopcheck(void)
+{
+	if (loopcheck_clear_open())
+		cancel_delayed_work_sync(&loopcheck.work);
 }
 
 void complete_kernel_loopcheck(void)
